## Goal
Address the automated Claude review findings on the DEV-47 "ask target" PR (#15). Document the limits of the "Remember" feature, clarify a code comment, and cover the `RememberKey` edge cases in tests.

## Problems
The review pointed out that a remembered rule is narrower than users might assume. It pins only the host and the meeting path, so a rule written by "Remember" does not constrain which app opened the link or its working directory. The docs did not say so. A "joined duplicate" in `cmd/portero/app.go` was also unexplained. `RememberKey` edge cases, such as format characters in the host or path, lacked test coverage.

## Decision
- `docs/rules.md`: added a bullet under "Remember" stating that only the host and meeting path are pinned and that opener and cwd are not.
- `cmd/portero/app.go`: added a comment explaining why the joined duplicate exists.
- `internal/rules/rules_test.go`: added tests for the `RememberKey` edge cases.

These are documentation and test changes only. No behaviour changes, and `make test` passes.

